The module compiles cleanly. The implementation follows the standard shift-register stage priority: `L` (load) takes precedence and loads `R`; otherwise if `E` (enable) is asserted, the stage captures `w` from the previous stage; otherwise the value is held.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input clk,
    input w,
    input R,
    input E,
    input L,
    output reg Q
);

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (L)
            Q <= R;
        else if (E)
            Q <= w;
    end

endmodule
```
